                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab37255a-684d-30f1-b990-7a7d12b62645",
                        "entry_id": "7df5bf54-da61-3801-8cee-e3c11c028854",
                        "glosses": [
                            "связанный, соотносящийся по значению с существительным агиография"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a37b421f-33a1-4660-9dbf-2a62122aee04",
                                "sense_id": "ab37255a-684d-30f1-b990-7a7d12b62645",
                                "text": "Литературный язык XVI в. в произведениях церковно-богословских, агиографических и исторических жанров характеризуется выспренней патетикой и пристрастием к церковнославянизмам, в чём обнаруживается развитие и углубление стилистических традиций, унаследованных от предыдущего столетия, но и в эти жанры порой проникают живая народная речь и образные средства живого народного языка."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "067b9a4e-da6a-4b57-999f-63fc991e65a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "7df5bf54-da61-3801-8cee-e3c11c028854",
                        "source_sense_id": "ab37255a-684d-30f1-b990-7a7d12b62645",
                        "target_lang_word": "hagiographic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hagiographic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e609d739-bef6-3f1a-94d0-93ed23e51d3d",
                                        "entry_id": "74456b3b-25be-3001-abfe-818cc23e06c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to hagiography."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edf8f3f2-8927-4e00-9ef6-1542352d906c",
                                                "sense_id": "e609d739-bef6-3f1a-94d0-93ed23e51d3d",
                                                "text": "But the stakes are clearly higher than in the hagiographic viewpoint expressed in [Girard, 1971] and a change of syntax (as the one coming from linear logic) may occur from disturbing semantics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e87897d-a603-34cb-9ec0-ff9420e1b7f1",
                                        "entry_id": "74456b3b-25be-3001-abfe-818cc23e06c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Uncritically reverent; adulating."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d554b7f-bf6e-43db-898a-703455b36b3d",
                                                "sense_id": "3e87897d-a603-34cb-9ec0-ff9420e1b7f1",
                                                "text": "“Chairman Xi is a world leader. His book on governance has sold out in many countries across the world,” Zhong gushed, parroting the unashamedly hagiographic bulletins in which the party news agency Xinhua excels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "119b2eeb-e4ec-450d-8eab-98bf285d253d",
                        "source_entry_id": "7df5bf54-da61-3801-8cee-e3c11c028854",
                        "source_sense_id": "ab37255a-684d-30f1-b990-7a7d12b62645",
                        "target_lang_word": "hagiographical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hagiographical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cbed2e2-18fe-32a1-b544-81abd4775b3b",
                                        "entry_id": "ac4b1cdb-7551-39b3-bb81-2ca8dddace1c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "hagiographic"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "299126cb-ee0e-46a7-b57e-bf398f49e7e3",
                                                "sense_id": "0cbed2e2-18fe-32a1-b544-81abd4775b3b",
                                                "text": "Saladin's prophetic namesake, by any account as obviously an antiwarrior as one can imagine, seems at first too antithetical a character for comparison with the anti-Crusader par excellence, and therein lies the hagiographical dynamic at work."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7692a803-43d8-4b83-b803-45d0d2d78655",
                        "source_entry_id": "7df5bf54-da61-3801-8cee-e3c11c028854",
                        "source_sense_id": "ab37255a-684d-30f1-b990-7a7d12b62645",
                        "target_lang_word": "hagiographisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hagiographisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b70a604a-3b1c-33cc-bae9-ec7857b8452b",
                                        "entry_id": "a909d132-ea5f-3dca-980c-928eff3f175e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "auf die Hagiografie/Hagiographie (die Erforschung und Beschreibung von Heiligenleben) bezogen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4154f187-c6eb-43ea-8dc4-21028cbf4632",
                                                "sense_id": "b70a604a-3b1c-33cc-bae9-ec7857b8452b",
                                                "text": "„Sie zeigte sich auch im 20. Jahrhundert in den beiden klassischen Cortés-Biographien des Spaniers Salvador de Madariaga und des Mexikaners Carlos Pereyra (1942), die beide eine hagiographische Tendenz aufweisen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
